# Everything is LF in the working tree too, whatever core.autocrlf says. Git for
# Windows installs with autocrlf=true, and a CRLF checkout broke three things there
# (measured 2026-10-16): Biome's formatter (LF) failed every source file, start.sh /
# install.sh got `\r` in their shebang and function bodies, and the fixtures the
# tests patch with "\n"-anchored edits stopped matching. The rules below override this
# one for the files that need CRLF.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Windows launchers MUST keep CRLF. cmd.exe mis-parses a LF-only .cmd (a trailing
# LF can swallow the last line, and `goto`/`if` blocks break), so pin them rather
# than leaving it to the checkout's core.autocrlf.
*.cmd text eol=crlf
*.ps1 text eol=crlf

# The macOS/Linux launchers must stay LF — CRLF would make the shebang line read
# as `#!/usr/bin/env bash\r` and fail with "bad interpreter".
*.command text eol=lf
*.sh text eol=lf
